<HelpTab>
    <FluentText>
        Admins and Managers edit a dashboard by selecting it on the <a href="/manage/dashboards">Dashboards</a> list. It opens
        in preview, showing exactly what people will see.
    </FluentText>

    <HelpSection Title="Editing the layout">
        <ol>
            <li>Select the preview button in the toolbar to switch to editing.</li>
            <li>Use the + button to add a widget.</li>
            <li>Use the arrows above a widget to move it, and the + and − buttons to make it wider or narrower and
                the up and down buttons to make it shorter or taller. The grid is 12 columns wide. A widget that's moved
                or grown into another one pushes it down out of the way.</li>
            <li>Select the cog above a widget to change its settings.</li>
            <li>Select the dashboard's name to rename it.</li>
            <li>Select <strong>Save</strong>. Nothing is kept until you do.</li>
        </ol>
        <FluentText>
            Buttons and controls on widgets only work in preview. Widgets for features your location doesn't have
            are hidden in preview, but still shown while editing so you can remove them.
        </FluentText>
        <HelpNote Intent="MessageBarIntent.Warning">
            Deleting a dashboard can't be undone. If it was everyone's home screen, people go back to the
            standard home page.
        </HelpNote>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="Show a widget only at certain times">
        <ol>
            <li>While editing, select the eye button on the widget (<strong>Show only when…</strong>).</li>
            <li>Press <strong>Add condition</strong> and choose one: <strong>Time of day is between</strong>,
                <strong>Day of week is</strong>, <strong>A kiosk is or isn't in a game</strong>, or
                <strong>A location is open or closed</strong>. Add more if you need to; the widget shows only while
                all of them are true.</li>
            <li>Press <strong>Done</strong>, then <strong>Save</strong> the dashboard.</li>
        </ol>
        <FluentText>
            For example, a closing checklist on the laser kiosk shown only between 18:00 and 23:59. While a widget is hidden
            its space stays empty, so nothing else on the dashboard moves. Times and days are UK venue time. A widget with
            conditions shows an <strong>Only…</strong> badge while editing, and the editor always shows every widget.
        </FluentText>
    </HelpSection>
</HelpTab>
